// Typecheck contract for test files.
//
// The base tsconfig excludes **/*.test.ts, so for years nothing type-checked a
// test fixture. A shared type could gain a required field and every stale
// fixture stayed silent until its assertions failed with a confusing mismatch —
// or, worse, kept passing against a value the type no longer allows.
//
// This config type-checks tests too, minus a frozen list of files that were
// already failing when the check was introduced. The list is debt, not policy:
// it only ever shrinks. Delete entries as the files are fixed; never add one to
// make a new failure go away, because every file not listed here is protected
// and adding to the list gives that protection up.
//
// Nothing runs this config directly. Sources plus every test file is a large
// enough program to exhaust Node's default heap on a CI runner, so the check is
// split across tsconfig.tests.server.json and tsconfig.tests.client.json, which
// inherit this exclusion list and each compile one half. `npm run check:tests`
// runs both.
//
// `incremental` is off deliberately: the base config points tsBuildInfoFile at a
// single path in node_modules, and sharing it would let these runs and `npm run
// check` overwrite each other's build info and return results that depend on
// which ran last.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "incremental": false
  },
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "build",
    "dist",
